<title>INDIA: Indian soybean demand looks up, soyoil, meal slip.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean demand looks up, soyoil, meal slip.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in central Indian markets on Monday but demand appeared to be firming up with processing plants showing buying interest also at higher prices, dealers said.</p>
<p>Arrival was around 10,000 tonnes on Monday, just half of daily arrivals last year at the same time.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell sharply on heavy selling from processing plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent prices were down by 400 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soyoil refined was down by 500 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soymeal was bearish in a tradeless market. Soymeal yellow was $267 for ready shipment and was $265-266 for January shipment. Rapeseed extraction was $135 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR Bhavnagar.</p>
